# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  liki — privacy-by-default .gitignore
#
#  Everything under wiki/, inbox/, and assets/ is PRIVATE by default: it is
#  ignored here and never leaves your machine except via your own cloud sync
#  (e.g. iCloud). Git tracks only what you explicitly allowlist below.
#
#  `install-wiki` rewrites the PUBLIC ALLOWLIST block once you choose which
#  domains to make public. Until then, NOTHING under wiki/ is committed —
#  a clone that gets pushed before setup can never leak a private note.
#
#  ORDER MATTERS: gitignore is last-match-wins. The `*.local.md` rule is kept
#  as the FINAL line on purpose, so it overrides every allowlist above it and
#  a `.local.md` note can never be committed — not even inside a public domain.
#  Do not add anything after it.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
.trash/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ── Vault content: private by default ──
wiki/*
inbox/*
assets/*
index.md
log.md

# Keep the empty vault skeleton present on a fresh clone
!wiki/.gitkeep

# Always-public drop zones (only ever hold public, non-personal files)
!inbox/public/
!inbox/public/**
!assets/public/
!assets/public/**

# ── Obsidian: ship app + plugin config, not layout/hotkeys ──
.obsidian/*
!.obsidian/app.json
!.obsidian/core-plugins.json
!.obsidian/community-plugins.json

# Ship the Anki-card callout styling (only this snippet — not the user's own).
# Re-include the dir, re-ignore its contents, then re-include the one file.
!.obsidian/snippets/
.obsidian/snippets/*
!.obsidian/snippets/anki-cards.css

# ── PUBLIC ALLOWLIST ──
# install-wiki writes your chosen public wiki/ domains here. Example, to make
# a Technical domain public (mirrors the template author's own setup):
#     !wiki/Technical/
#     !wiki/Technical/**
# Add your `!wiki/<Domain>/` re-includes in THIS block, above the *.local.md
# line — never below it.
# <to_be_determined_from_install_skill>

# ── Convention: *.local.md is NEVER committed, anywhere — KEEP LAST ──
# Overrides every allowlist above so a sensitive note stays private even inside
# a public domain. Nothing may follow this line.
*.local.md
